# {{.Name}} ({{.Type}})

{{ .Description | trimspace }}

This resource owns every SDK Authentication key for one Braze app. Remote keys
omitted from `keys` are deleted on apply. Use one collection resource per app;
do not also manage that app's keys through singular resources, another collection
resource, or another Terraform state. Use resource `for_each` for multiple apps.
The API's `app_group` path prefix does not change the per-app ownership scope.

To manage selected keys while leaving other keys unmanaged, use
`braze_sdk_authentication_key` instead.

This resource registers public keys only. Keep private keys with the JWT issuer;
SDK integration and enforcement are configured separately using the
[Braze SDK Authentication guide](https://www.braze.com/docs/developer_guide/sdk_integration/authentication/).
The REST API key needs `sdk_authentication.create`, `sdk_authentication.keys`,
`sdk_authentication.primary`, and `sdk_authentication.delete` for the full lifecycle.

~> **Existing keys require import.** Creating this resource requires an empty
remote collection. Import the app first if it already has registered keys, then
configure every key you intend to keep before applying.

